  "section_id": "s08-latitude",
  "text": "Distance from the Equator (Latitudes). The Earth is divided into imaginary lines called latitudes. Places near the equator receive direct sunlight throughout the year, making them hot. As we move towards the poles, sunlight spreads out, making these areas cooler. This is why tropical regions are warm, while polar regions are cold.",
